G40-203 — 101-guide copy, HELD until the in-app screen ships
=============================================================

WHAT THIS IS
  The two 101-guide edits for the self-service phone-number change. They are
  correct and reviewed, and they are NOT in the working tree on purpose.

WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT AN EDIT
  `gopher-go-101.html` currently tells users their phone number "can't be
  changed". That is TRUE today and becomes false the moment the app build
  ships. The guide describes what the product does, not what it will do
  (standing rule 5), so the copy cannot land early.

  ⚠️ AND "just leave it uncommitted" IS NOT A HOLD — that is what this file
  exists to correct. `scripts/deploy.sh` reads the WORKING TREE: a dirty
  `Final/` BLOCKS every clean site deploy for every session, and the only way
  past that refusal is `--allow-dirty`, which SHIPS the dirty file. Held
  uncommitted, these two files were simultaneously blocking everyone's deploys
  and one `--allow-dirty` away from publishing copy about a screen users cannot
  reach. Another session came within one flag of doing exactly that on
  2026-09-08. The standing-rules table lists "uncommitted in the working tree"
  as genuinely held; on this repo that is misleading, and out-of-tree is the
  real hold.

WHEN TO APPLY
  After the store build carrying G40-203 ships — i.e. when Account → Change
  Phone Number actually exists in the live apps.

      git apply docs/handoff/G40-203-101-guides.patch

  It applies on top of G40-304's guide edits (different sections; verified
  non-overlapping — theirs are #active / the safety list, these are #profile).

WHAT IT CONTAINS
  gopher-go-101.html      — corrects the false "phone number can't be changed"
                            claim, and adds a "Changing your phone number"
                            subsection under #profile.
  gopher-request-101.html — the parallel subsection.

Both were rendered and verified at 375x812 before being held.

